@page "/docs/installation"
@layout Layout.DocsLayout

<PageTitle>Installation · Klyroo.UI</PageTitle>
<div class="pg-prose">
    <p class="pg-eyebrow">Getting started</p>
    <h1>Installation</h1>
    <p class="pg-lead">Add the package, register the services, and load one stylesheet.</p>

    <h2>1. Add the package</h2>
    <CodeBlock Code="dotnet add package Klyroo.UI --prerelease" />

    <h2>2. Register the services</h2>
    <p>Call <code>AddKlyrooUi</code> in the server <code>Program.cs</code> and in the client one, with the same configuration. A shared method in the client project keeps them in sync.</p>
    <CodeBlock Title="Program.cs" Code="@ProgramCs" />

    <h2>3. Load the styles</h2>
    <p>Without Tailwind in your app, load the precompiled stylesheet and its reset:</p>
    <CodeBlock Title="App.razor" Code="@AppRazor" />
    <p>With Tailwind v4 in your app, each build copies the Klyroo.UI theme to <code>obj/klyroo/klyroo.theme.css</code>. Import it after Tailwind:</p>
    <CodeBlock Title="app.css" Code="@AppCss" />
    <p>No Node needed: <code>&lt;KlyrooTailwind&gt;true&lt;/KlyrooTailwind&gt;</code> compiles that stylesheet at build time with the Tailwind standalone CLI. See the <a href="/docs/tailwind">Tailwind</a> guide.</p>

    <h2>4. Use the components</h2>
    <CodeBlock Title="_Imports.razor" Code="@("@using Klyroo.UI")" />
    <p>Remove Bootstrap from the Blazor template, or import it in a cascade layer: CSS outside layers overrides Tailwind's.</p>

    <h2>Sister packages</h2>
    <p>
        <code>Klyroo.Table</code> (and the packages after it) <strong>require Tailwind compiled by your app</strong>. Their stylesheet is not precompiled: a second precompiled sheet would repeat utilities after
        <code>klyroo.css</code> and override its responsive and dark variants. Add the package and turn on <code>&lt;KlyrooTailwind&gt;true&lt;/KlyrooTailwind&gt;</code>, and the build imports the package's classes for you.
        With your own Tailwind, import <code>obj/klyroo/klyroo-table.theme.css</code> after the Klyroo.UI theme and set <code>KlyrooToolsOwnTailwind</code> to <code>true</code> to silence the warning <code>KLYTOOLS001</code>.
        See the <a href="/docs/tailwind">Tailwind</a> guide.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock Title="app.css (your own Tailwind)" Code="@ToolsCss" />
    <p>A sister package and Klyroo.UI must have the same version: <code>Klyroo.Table</code> depends on exactly the version of Klyroo.UI it was built with.</p>

    <h2>Server rendering: Klyroo.UI.Server</h2>
    <p>
        A component that renders without a browser, in a static render or a prerender, can read what the browser left in a cookie: the data list uses the time zone cookie so its date filters cut the days of the user.
        <code>Klyroo.UI</code> is also loaded by WebAssembly and MAUI apps, where there is no ASP.NET Core request, so it only knows <code>IKlyRequestCookies</code>; the package <code>Klyroo.UI.Server</code> implements it.
        Add it to the <strong>server</strong> project and call <code>AddKlyrooServer()</code> in its <code>Program.cs</code> (never in a WebAssembly client). Without it a static or prerendered data list cuts days in UTC until the
        browser is interactive, and Development logs one warning that says so.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock Title="Program.cs (server project)" Code="@ServerCs" />
    <p>The package has the same version as Klyroo.UI and depends on exactly that version.</p>

    <h2>MAUI Blazor Hybrid apps</h2>
    <p>
        In a MAUI app the package and the stylesheets are the same, but there are no render modes and no server. Call <code>AddKlyrooUi</code>
        from <code>MauiProgram.cs</code> (after <code>AddMauiBlazorWebView</code>), link <code>_content/Klyroo.UI/klyroo.preflight.css</code> and
        <code>klyroo.css</code> from <code>wwwroot/index.html</code>, and add <code>HeadOutlet</code> as a root component so <code>KlyHead</code> can
        write the theme and fonts into the head. The <a href="/docs/maui">MAUI and Blazor Hybrid</a> guide has the details and the status of each platform.
    </p>
</div>

@code {
    private const string ProgramCs = """
        builder.Services.AddKlyrooUi(options =>
        {
            options.Button.Slot("base", "font-semibold");
        });
        """;

    private const string AppRazor = """
        <head>
            <KlyColorModeScript />
            <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["_content/Klyroo.UI/klyroo.preflight.css"]" />
            <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["_content/Klyroo.UI/klyroo.css"]" />
        </head>
        """;

    private const string ServerCs = """
        // dotnet add package Klyroo.UI.Server --prerelease
        builder.Services.AddKlyrooUi();
        builder.Services.AddKlyrooTable();
        builder.Services.AddKlyrooServer();   // calls AddHttpContextAccessor and registers IKlyRequestCookies
        """;

    private const string ToolsCss = """
        @import "tailwindcss";
        @import "../obj/klyroo/klyroo.theme.css";
        @import "../obj/klyroo/klyroo-table.theme.css";
        """;

    private const string AppCss = """
        @import "tailwindcss";
        @import "../obj/klyroo/klyroo.theme.css";
        """;
}
